            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Mandela's Leadership in the ANC</strong><br>\nAs a leader in the ANC, Mandela helped form the ANC Youth League, which advocated for a more radical approach to fighting apartheid. He rose through the ranks to become the president of the ANC in 1951 and emphasized the necessity for armed resistance after the Sharpeville Massacre, where peaceful protesters were shot by police.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Rivonia Trial</strong><br>\nIn 1962, Mandela was arrested for conspiring to overthrow the state and was sentenced to life imprisonment following the Rivonia Trial. His statement during the trial, where he said he was prepared to die for the democratic ideal of a free and equal society, became a defining moment in the struggle against apartheid.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Years in Prison</strong><br>\nMandela spent 27 years in prison, much of it on Robben Island, where he became a symbol of the anti-apartheid movement. He used his time in prison to further his education and remained a leader among his incarcerated peers. Despite the harsh conditions, Mandela's resolve to end apartheid did not wane.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
